==== hyperbricks yaml {!{detail_api}} ====
detail_api:
  - type: api_render
  - endpoint: https://example.com/catalog
  - method: GET
  - querykeys: [id]
  - response_status:
      enabled: true
      required: true
      priority: 100
      map: {"404": 404, "503": 503, "409": ignore}
  - inline: '{{if eq .Status 404}}Item not found{{else}}{{.Data.name}}{{end}}'
==== explainer ====
This API instance explicitly participates in the enclosing response status. Actual decoded upstream 404 and 503 responses propose mapped statuses; 409 proposes nothing. Required failures outrank valid mappings. Declare the policy explicitly again when directly inheriting this API definition.
==== expected json ====
{
  "@type": "<API_RENDER>",
  "endpoint": "https://example.com/catalog",
  "method": "GET",
  "querykeys": ["id"],
  "response_status": {
    "enabled": true,
    "required": true,
    "priority": 100,
    "map": {"404": 404, "503": 503, "409": "ignore"}
  },
  "inline": "{{if eq .Status 404}}Item not found{{else}}{{.Data.name}}{{end}}"
}
